Getting a professional website shouldn't be complicated, expensive, or slow. That's the principle behind our [managed starter website service](/services/managed-starter-websites/) — and the Electrician Merthyr Tydfil project is a good example of it working exactly as it should.

A local electrician needed to get online properly. They had the skills, the experience, and the customers — but no website, no Google presence, and no easy way for new customers to find them. They didn't want a long process or a big upfront bill. They wanted to be online, quickly, with a site that actually did something.

## The Brief

A professional online presence, affordable and fast. The site needed to cover all core services — domestic electrical work, commercial, inspection and testing, and emergency call-outs — and rank for the searches that local homeowners and businesses make when they need an electrician.

## What We Built

A fully managed website under our Managed Starter Website service. The site includes:

- Dedicated service pages for domestic, commercial, inspection, and emergency electrical work
- An "Areas We Serve" section targeting Merthyr Tydfil and the surrounding South Wales locations
- Clear calls to action on every page — quote request forms, click-to-call phone number, and email contact
- Google Business Profile optimisation to support local map rankings alongside the website
- Fast, SEO-ready hosting with SSL and daily backups — all included in the monthly plan

Our streamlined process allowed us to produce a professional result quickly and cost-effectively. The site was live within days of the brief being agreed.

## The Results

- Professional online presence live within days of briefing
- Ranks for local electrician search terms in Merthyr Tydfil and surrounding areas
- Generates enquiries consistently through quote forms and direct phone/email contact

For a tradesperson who needed to get online quickly and affordably, the result is a site that looks the part, works on every device, and quietly generates leads in the background while they're on the job.

